WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.089
Loop X two point zero. A workbench for
long-horizon research.

2
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.189
Carry the goal, constraints, and return
route.

3
00:00:10.369 --> 00:00:12.440
Let the existing owner adopt the work.

4
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.602
Keep corrections on the task. Return the
evidence.

5
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.287
See work, waiting decisions, and schedules.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.586
Can a linear gate miss a useful nonlinear
model?

7
00:00:25.766 --> 00:00:28.330
Keep both explanations open until the test.

8
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:35.239
On the thirty percent duplication probe,
accuracy rose from forty one point two to
eighty five percent.

9
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.545
On the independent control, accuracy stayed
the same.

10
00:00:40.725 --> 00:00:42.595
Time increased thirty two percent.

11
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.757
A linear gate cannot rule out all nonlinear
headroom.

12
00:00:47.937 --> 00:00:51.952
Keep the candidate eligible. Its native
score benefit is still unknown.

13
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.348
Keep the finding, the control, and the
reason for the next test.

14
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.346
Read six process judgments. Keep unknowns
visible.

15
00:01:01.526 --> 00:01:05.172
Trace claims to their source. Measure
results and costs separately.

16
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.704
Use a matched native test. Record the full
cost.

17
00:01:10.884 --> 00:01:12.780
Do not promote an untested claim.

18
00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.630
Keep the next step with its evidence.

19
00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.633
Loop X. Keep the research, evidence, and
next decision together.
